<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto von Bismarck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1898">1898</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Bismarck</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto von Bismarck was a Prussian statesman who unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and served as the first chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. He built a federal constitution that preserved Prussian dominance among the empire's constituent states. He fought the Catholic Church in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulturkampf">Kulturkampf</a>, opposed socialism, and introduced the world's first national <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-insurance">social insurance</a> system in the 1880s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck.jpg" alt="Otto von Bismarck" width="311" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_von_Bismarck_1885_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
